        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "cd0b4009-fd08-3a7f-923d-e33cc882f401",
                "word": "colorisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e77115e0-1a6d-4be7-98f2-29bd7cdbf26a",
                        "entry_id": "cd0b4009-fd08-3a7f-923d-e33cc882f401",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "colorismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce1f3e5a-7c29-35f5-b94f-f8e8616c8fde",
                        "entry_id": "cd0b4009-fd08-3a7f-923d-e33cc882f401",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Discrimination fondée sur les variations d’intensité de la couleur de la peau des personnes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa4deae1-f075-45dc-9589-f90b4a9de150",
                                "sense_id": "ce1f3e5a-7c29-35f5-b94f-f8e8616c8fde",
                                "text": "Nous entendons souvent parler des luttes contre le racisme des blancs envers les minorités. Des manifestations, des débats et de nombreux articles traitent de ce sujet, mais pourquoi ne parle-t-on pas du colorisme qui est une forme de « racisme » au sein d’une même communauté ?|"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "750588b3-6f5c-4b50-9628-567a1081acbc",
                                "sense_id": "ce1f3e5a-7c29-35f5-b94f-f8e8616c8fde",
                                "text": "Je sais qu’au cours de mes études supérieures et que, du fait de mon intérêt pour la littérature, j’ai déjà entendu le terme “bounty” à mon propos. Et plus j’y pense, plus le terme en lui-même est à la croisée de plusieurs axes tels que le classisme, le racisme et le colorisme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a55a0337-1c67-4bb1-a5f6-5291e5181384",
                                "sense_id": "ce1f3e5a-7c29-35f5-b94f-f8e8616c8fde",
                                "text": "En France comme aux Etats-Unis, des milliers de femmes et d’hommes sont marqués par ce qu’on nomme le colorisme, une discrimination favorisant les peaux plus pâles."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc3f1415-aad7-331c-96fd-0ba468961291",
                        "entry_id": "cd0b4009-fd08-3a7f-923d-e33cc882f401",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Coloris, colorisation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0b01531-9f3e-465f-978c-543e96a3efcc",
                                "sense_id": "fc3f1415-aad7-331c-96fd-0ba468961291",
                                "text": "Le colorisme joue sur le mélange des couleurs fondamentales, de nombreuses nuances donnent à l'ensemble une plus grande unité et font ressortir les parties importantes de l'image."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6c0538d-eebd-4666-b676-a79a3494c4ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "cd0b4009-fd08-3a7f-923d-e33cc882f401",
                        "source_sense_description": "racisme",
                        "target_lang_word": "colorism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "colorism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                        "entry_id": "9bed6a2e-26d7-3345-afab-a6dc5eb4004a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prejudice or bias against persons on the basis of their skin color or complexion, often among persons of the same racial identification."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c03e0320-5bef-4cd4-b384-d52f3206775c",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "Black America used to be, and perhaps still is, a pigmentocracy, which means that the social hierarchy is based largely on colorism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c28956f-9f76-4752-8511-18fea3b5e40e",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "This type of preferential colorism isn’t only found in the church aisles, it’s at family gatherings, on the dating scene, in the classroom, on the playground—it’s everywhere."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fed844ff-c72a-4c81-a993-6cd2ad206f4a",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "Colorism from your own people feels worse than racism – at the very least your own family and people should welcome you, no?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43079cb1-6ecd-4488-a830-058ced94ba72",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "Eliminating racism and colorism is, of course, a worthy pursuit, but it’s also impossible to do in the abstract."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "935c5ba1-0c59-4906-a867-02cc13a93505",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "Like those, James’s season still gave noticeably less screen time to its Black contestants—and because of James’s Blackness, the colorism that has always plagued The Bachelor became more visible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ef80f85-74c8-4d79-906e-2d25b96b8552",
                                                "sense_id": "c2b7d225-a4a4-3b20-b1c3-640084999f10",
                                                "text": "Like many other parts of the world, colourism is rampant in India."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd2bdbc7-524a-3336-aac5-662956f33e6a",
                                        "entry_id": "9bed6a2e-26d7-3345-afab-a6dc5eb4004a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A style of painting characterised by the use of intense color."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3a439d7-4c9d-46a2-b8cc-4c1ac66a0f91",
                                                "sense_id": "fd2bdbc7-524a-3336-aac5-662956f33e6a",
                                                "text": "Turner's colorism with its cosmic world view had nothing to do with realism, in spite of its impasto handling of colour. […] Turner's images are based on the far-sighted and purely objective views of the 18th century which he imbued with new meaning through his colorism based on colour theory and plein-air painting."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
